  "articleBody": "When your house suffers fire damage, there are a lot of misconceptions floating around that can make the cleanup process even more confusing. Let's bust a few myths to help you understand things better. Myth: You can just paint over smoke odors. Fact: Painting over smoke odors without proper remediation is like putting a band-aid on a broken bone. The smell will eventually seep back through. Odor molecules need to be neutralized and removed from affected materials. Myth: All fire damage cleanup is the same. Fact: Not at all! The type of fire, materials burned, and extent of smoke penetration all impact the cleanup process. A small kitchen fire is vastly different from widespread structural damage. Myth: You should clean everything yourself immediately. Fact: Jumping in without the right tools or knowledge can actually cause more damage. Improper cleaning can permanently embed soot into surfaces or spread contamination. Myth: Your home will never smell ",
